# Illustrative SKOS terminology for the GrainCorp elevation-capacity example ([[R211]]).
#
# The port scheme is BORROWED from stem-terms.ttl, deliberately and verbatim: the same
# publisher prints both documents, and the seven prefLabels below are exactly the seven port
# labels the capacity page's spanning header draws (MEASURED against the page, not assumed).
# Borrowing rather than re-deriving is what lets `marker_field` ground a split key by UNIQUE
# scheme admission — the same oracle, the same scheme, a second document.
#
# WHETHER THIS IS THE RIGHT AUTHORITY for a capacity table is a vocabulary question, and the
# spec records it as open (§ 6): these are a shipping stem's ports, and a capacity table's
# ports happen to be the same set. Nothing here asserts that they must be.
#
# Port names are public third-party nomenclature; the source document itself is NOT
# redistributed here, and no commercially identifying data appears in this vocabulary.
@prefix ship: <https://example.org/shipping#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

ship:scheme-port a skos:ConceptScheme ; skos:prefLabel "Export ports"@en .
ship:p-mackay     a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme ship:scheme-port ; skos:prefLabel "Mackay"@en .
ship:p-gladstone  a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme ship:scheme-port ; skos:prefLabel "Gladstone"@en .
ship:p-fisherman  a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme ship:scheme-port ; skos:prefLabel "Fisherman Islands"@en .
ship:p-carrington a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme ship:scheme-port ; skos:prefLabel "Carrington"@en .
ship:p-kembla     a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme ship:scheme-port ; skos:prefLabel "Port Kembla"@en .
ship:p-geelong    a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme ship:scheme-port ; skos:prefLabel "Geelong"@en .
ship:p-portland   a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme ship:scheme-port ; skos:prefLabel "Portland"@en .
